\name{dpgof-package}
\alias{dpgof-package}
\alias{dpgof}
\title{Distance-profile goodness-of-fit tests}
\description{Multiplier bootstrap tests for distributions on metric spaces. See the README for installation, a short example, and links to article reproduction instructions.}
\details{
The active article results use the restricted spiked normal, normal with scalar
covariance, multivariate normal, logistic Gaussian, von Mises--Fisher,
hyperbolic von Mises--Fisher, cardioid, small-circle, and uniform--beta
models. The associated effective runners and saved results are indexed in
\file{paper/README.md}.

The wrappers \code{multiplier_bootstrap_jp},
\code{multiplier_bootstrap_beta_mixture2},
\code{multiplier_bootstrap_logitnormal_mixture2},
\code{multiplier_bootstrap_spherical_cauchy},
\code{multiplier_bootstrap_watson},
\code{multiplier_bootstrap_axial_truncnorm_mixture2}, and
\code{multiplier_bootstrap_logistic_gaussian_sigma_shape} are retained for
exploratory analyses. They are not among the effective runners for the active
article tables or figures and have less validation against those results.
}
